# It's me - spiritual (Standing in the Need of Prayer)
# Traditioneel: Hymnary.org vermeldt "Standing in the Need of Prayer" als
# Afro-Amerikaanse spiritual zonder bekende auteur, in 82 gezangboeken. Publiek domein.
# Overgenomen uit ITS.ME (WordPerfect 5.1, 1991). Tikfout hersteld: "deakon" werd
# "deacon"; "apreaching" gelaten (a-preaching). De bron zet "Refrein:" boven de
# eerste zes regels; alleen de eerste twee zijn het refrein, de vier daarna het eerste
# couplet. Het refrein is na elk couplet herhaald. De aanwijzing over een andere versie
# van het laatste couplet staat als opmerking. Akkoorden alleen bij refrein en eerste
# couplet, volgens de kolommen.
{title: It's me}
{meta: id it-s-me}
{meta: language en}
{lyricist: traditioneel}
{composer: traditioneel}
{copyright: Public domain}
{meta: license public-domain}
{meta: source Overgenomen uit ITS.ME (WordPerfect 5.1, 1991); herkomst via Hymnary.org}
{meta: tag kampvuur}
{meta: tag geestelijk}
{key: Em}

{start_of_chorus}
[Em]It's me, it's me, [C]it's me my Lord, Stan[D]ding in the [G]need of prayer
[Em]It's me, [B]it's me, it's [Em]me my Lord[C], Standing [D7]in the nee[G]d of prayer
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse}
Not [Em]my father, not my mother, [B]but it's me [Em]my Lord
[C]Standing in the need [D]of praye[G]r
Not [Em]my father, not my [B]mother, but [Em]it's me my Lord
[C]Standing in the need [D7]of praye[G]r
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse}
Not my uncle, not my aunt, but it's me my Lord
Standing in the need of prayer
Not my uncle, not my aunt, but it's me my Lord
Standing in the need of prayer
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse}
Not my neighbour, not a stranger, but it's me my Lord
Standing in the need of prayer
Not my neighbour, not a stranger, but it's me my Lord
Standing in the need of prayer
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse}
Not my preacher, not my teacher, but it's me my Lord
Standing in the need of prayer
Not my preacher, not my teacher, but it's me my Lord
Standing in the need of prayer
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse}
Not my brother, not my sister, but it's me my Lord
Standing in the need of prayer
Not my brother, not my sister, but it's me my Lord
Standing in the need of prayer
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse}
Not the deacon who's apreaching, but it's me my Lord
Standing in the need of prayer
Not the deacon who's apreaching, but it's me my Lord
Standing in the need of prayer
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{comment: Andere versie van het laatste couplet}

{start_of_verse}
Not my deacon, not my elder, but it's me my Lord
Standing in the need of prayer
Not the deacon who's apreaching, but it's me my Lord
Standing in the need of prayer
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
